{
  "requirement": "The view of {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.index.file_map.notes` MUST use\nthe current workspace source at book-render time and explicitly identify its\ncontents as current workspace source notes.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has two obligations: the file-notes view must use the current workspace source at book-render time, and it must explicitly identify its contents as current workspace source notes.\n\nBoth are covered by `src/execution_coverage/notes.rs#mod[tests]/fn[each_render_reads_current_notes_and_keeps_recorded_reviews_without_writing]`, which carries a `{test}` reference to the subject.\n\n- **Current source at render time.**\n  - The test builds a fixture file containing a fenced citation with \"Original platform explanation.\"\n  - It renders once, rewrites `code.rs` on disk to say \"Updated platform explanation.\", and renders again.\n  - It asserts the second render contains the updated text.\n  - It asserts that the part of the content before \"Review:\" no longer contains the original text.\n  - This shows each render re-reads the workspace and does not reuse earlier content. It also rules out a stale snapshot taken when the first render ran. The `render` helper calls `pages` directly, so it reads at render time.\n- **Explicit identification.** The test asserts the content contains \"Current workspace source notes\". `fn[pages]` emits this as the bold label \"**Current workspace source notes**, read at book-render time.\" The assertion matches the requirement's wording, so a view that left out the label would fail it.\n\nOther assertions in the test cover the recorded review and the render-only behaviour, which belong to sibling requirements. They don't weaken the checks above.\n\nI found no unnamed boundary or failure case in the subject's text that lacks a test. The text has no SHOULD or alternative clauses, and the sibling notes behaviours (availability, reviews, justifications) are tested under their own requirements.",
